<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prato Cathedral</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cathedral of Santo Stefano, Prato</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prato Cathedral, dedicated to Santo Stefano, grew from the parish church around which the town developed and was enlarged from the 12th to the 15th century. It holds the relic of the Holy Girdle of the Virgin, shown from an external pulpit by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/donatello">Donatello</a> and Michelozzo, and frescoes by Filippo Lippi on the lives of Saint Stephen and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-the-baptist">John the Baptist</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prato-cathedral.jpg" alt="Prato Cathedral" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Massimilianogalardi · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duomo_Prato_01.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
